 commit_message="UPSTREAM: mmc: Allow forward compatibility for eMMC  As stated by the eMMC 5.0 specification, a chip should not be rejected only because of the revision stated in the EXT_CSD_REV field of the EXT_CSD register.  Remove the control on this value, the control of the CSD_STRUCTURE field should be sufficient to reject future incompatible changes.  Signed-off-by: Romain Izard &lt;romain.izard.pro@gmail.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Ulf Hansson &lt;ulf.hansson@linaro.org&gt; (cherry-picked from git-kernel.org torvalds/linux.git master  commit 03a59437ef6b6ad7fb0165cb9b96c08d6bf057fc)  BUG=chrome-os-partner:43566 TEST=try a newish(rev 8) emmc, should enumerate just fine  Change-Id: I42ec8b5138b564d0c3dff8f71423e3ae327f73c0 Signed-off-by: Alexandru M Stan &lt;amstan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/290353 Reviewed-by: Puthikorn Voravootivat &lt;puthik@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 303685bbd156d0d8be7a1ca81130e5834238bfae) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/317473 Commit-Ready: Anson Tseng &lt;anson.tseng@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: David Wu &lt;david_wu@quantatw.com&gt; Tested-by: Pan Sheng-Liang &lt;Sheng-Liang.Pan@quantatw.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Alexandru Stan &lt;amstan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="317473" owner_email="anson.tseng@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/73/317473/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I89a7d1b7403ee07e91708587e6ade9f9565035c2" commit="f7b8267a6ca2c641761afe005dd6d15515b0e124" commit_message="Disable HWTest for the &quot;toolchain-llvm&quot; builder.  This builder was configured to run the bvt-inline suite against pool:bvt.  This meant the builder was stealing time from DUTs needed to run release and PFQ testing.  Adding insult to injury, the builder has only ever been red, so the runs were failing mysteriously.  BUG=None TEST=unit tests  Change-Id: I89a7d1b7403ee07e91708587e6ade9f9565035c2 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/317576 Commit-Ready: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Matthew Sartori &lt;msartori@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="317576" owner_email="jrbarnette@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/76/317576/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8f1612ee153a412620bae5822d1b354ad8072916" commit="05a9e7df261f56ed457a2f1d081c08e7b8e97b20" commit_message="honeybuns: enable updates over USB-PD  Enable the RSA verification of the RW partition, so we are using the RW partition by default and the USB PD flashing VDMs are able to update the firmware over the Control Channel.  Signed-off-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt;  BRANCH=samus BUG=chrome-os-partner:47823 TEST=run the following sequence on a Samus connected to Honeybuns : ectool --name=cros_pd infopddev 1 ectool --name=cros_pd flashpd 5 1 ec.RW.bin ectool --name=cros_pd version and see the honeybuns properly updated and running the new version.  Change-Id: I8f1612ee153a412620bae5822d1b354ad8072916 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/312998 Commit-Ready: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="312998" owner_email="vpalatin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/98/312998/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I7c7e4a64554520237a1c9d2847f63ba0ee61ea46" commit="97d6a295f5aaff859b33404275af69f50dcf0dd0" commit_message="chromeos_config: testBoards now asserts, doesn't warn.  This unittest looks for configs that define multiple boards, which is MOSTLY an error. It was warning, not asserting before. Now it asserts, but has a WHITELIST of exceptions (currently with one entry).  BUG=chromium:568396 TEST=cbuildbot/chromeos_config_unittest  Change-Id: I7c7e4a64554520237a1c9d2847f63ba0ee61ea46 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/317274 Commit-Ready: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kevin Cheng &lt;kevcheng@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="317274" owner_email="dgarrett@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/74/317274/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I85eae412cb07d13f2f1eda49460faacf11bf393f" commit="19fae7085de6ed59b08ac8192a40e64d4d622a41" commit_message="[autotest] test_that checks autoserv return code.  If autoserv dies for unexpected reasons, test_that will exit with code 1.  TEST=test_that dummy_Pass HOST_IP test_that dummy_Fail HOST_IP force abstract_ssh to raise an exception so that autoserv will fail at crashinfo collection step. Check exit code is 1. BUG=chromium:555073  Change-Id: I85eae412cb07d13f2f1eda49460faacf11bf393f Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/317593 Commit-Ready: Fang Deng &lt;fdeng@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Fang Deng &lt;fdeng@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Fang Deng &lt;fdeng@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="317593" owner_email="fdeng@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url=